@meisterT I know you had a different opinion in the issue but I think the code has changed since that discussion.

We require some changes in the `.sh` files to make it compatible with all environments.

Deno task start was not compatible with Windows env, it is possible to use bash commands but most of the time it will bring lots of strange errors. so my idea was to create a separate task `start:beep`.

In `migration.ts` we are using two script files and they are directly calling `psql `command, which in some development environments we don't have direct access to the database. (For example, my database is not in my OS and I'm using a Docker container) 
We may have two options
1- Adding an ignore flag and checking the platform if it is not supported do it like the old days.
2- Using database protocols to communicate with a database, here is an example I found using https://deno.land/x/postgres/mod.ts  (Not sure about the performance)

```
async function exportTableToTSV(client: Client, table: string): Promise<void> {
    const result = await client.query(`COPY ${table} TO STDOUT WITH DELIMITER E'\t' CSV HEADER`);
    const rows = result.rows;
    if (rows.length > 0) {
        const tsvData = rows.map(row => row.join('\t')).join('\n');
        await writeTextFile(`${SEED_DIR}/${table}.tsv`, tsvData);
        console.log(`Exported table ${table} to ${SEED_DIR}/${table}.tsv`);
    } else {
        console.log(`Table ${table} is empty or does not exist.`);
    }
}

